{
  "title": "Neurilemmoma",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8053/neurilemmoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 4 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Neurilemmoma, also known as Schwannoma, are benign, encapsulated nerve sheath tumors composed of Schwann cells that occur on the surface of peripheral nerves.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition usually presents in patients in the 3rd to 6th decades of life with paresthesias in the distribution of the peripheral nerve.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with biopsy showing a lesion that is well encapsulated in a nerve sheath with histology showing verocay bodies. Immunostaining is positive for S100.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually observation for asymptomatic lesions. Marginal resection is recommended in cases of progressive symptoms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "peak incidence is in the **3rd to 6th decades**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "previous test question ages: 40, 45",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "affect males and females equally",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tumor is **well encapsulated** on the **surface of a peripheral nerve**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "often occurs on flexor surfaces of extremities and head and neck",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "larger lesions may occur in the pelvis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can affect motor or sensory nerves",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often associated with mutations affecting NF2 gene",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Malignant transformation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "extremely rare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually asymptomatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may have **paresthesia** in the distribution of the peripheral nerve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may have positive Tinel’s sign in the distribution of the nerve affected may be present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sequences",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "low intensity (dark) T1",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "high intensity (bright) on T2",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "diffuse enhancement with gadolinium",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may show “string sign”",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8053/images/string%20sign.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows string sign"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "difficult to differentiate from neurofibroma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Histology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Gross pathology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the lesion is well encapsulated in a nerve sheath",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8053/images/24a_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "gray in color",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8053/images/neurilemmoma10x02.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8053/images/antoni.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Antoni A structure**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a pattern of spindle cells arranged in intersecting bundles (**spindle cell battle formation**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8053/images/24b_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Antoni B**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "areas with less cellularity with loosely arranged cells",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Verocay bodies",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8053/images/verocay_diagram.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8053/images/verocay_histo.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**pathognomonic**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "composed of two rows of aligned nuclei in a palisading formation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Immunochemistry",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "strongly uniform S100 antibody staining",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "asymptomatic lesions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "marginal excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "symptoms or interfering with quality of life",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "nerve function may be preserved by careful dissection, excising the lesion parallel to the nerve fascicles so the lesion may be extruded.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "complications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "small risk of sensory deficits",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "recurrence is rare",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
